contempt|lack-of-respect|NOUN|strong disrespect|A strong feeling that someone or something deserves no respect.|sự khinh miệt; sự coi thường|His contempt for honest work shocked the other volunteers.|Sự coi thường công việc chân chính của anh khiến những tình nguyện viên khác sửng sốt.|Uncountable; contempt for someone or something, or treat someone with contempt.|0
contempt|court-disrespect|NOUN|disrespect for a court's authority|Behaviour that shows disrespect for a court or disobeys its authority.|hành vi coi thường tòa án; sự bất tuân đối với tòa án|The report said the witness had been found in contempt of court.|Bản tin cho biết nhân chứng đã bị xác định có hành vi coi thường tòa án.|Legal expression contempt of court; held or found in contempt. Exact legal consequences depend on the jurisdiction.|1
eligible|meeting-requirements|ADJECTIVE|meeting the requirements to take part|Meeting the conditions needed to receive something or take part in an activity.|đủ điều kiện; có tư cách tham gia|Volunteers who completed the training are eligible for this assignment.|Những tình nguyện viên đã hoàn tất khóa đào tạo đủ điều kiện nhận nhiệm vụ này.|Eligible for a benefit or role; eligible to do something. Eligibility concerns conditions, not certainty of selection.|0
inclusion|equal-participation|NOUN|enabling people to belong and participate|The practice of making people feel accepted and able to participate with others.|sự hòa nhập; việc tạo điều kiện tham gia bình đẳng|The club supports inclusion by offering instructions in several languages.|Câu lạc bộ hỗ trợ sự hòa nhập bằng cách cung cấp hướng dẫn bằng nhiều ngôn ngữ.|Usually uncountable; inclusion in a group or activity. This social sense is distinct from simply adding an item.|0
inclusion|adding-to-a-whole|NOUN|putting something into a larger whole|The act of putting something into a group, document, or other larger whole.|sự đưa vào; việc bổ sung vào|The editor approved the photograph's inclusion in the anniversary issue.|Biên tập viên chấp thuận việc đưa bức ảnh vào số báo kỷ niệm.|Usually uncountable; the inclusion of something in something names the item and its destination.|1
regain|get-back|VERB|get back what was lost|To get something back after losing it.|lấy lại; giành lại|The team regained the lead with a goal in the final minute.|Đội bóng giành lại vị trí dẫn trước bằng một bàn thắng ở phút cuối.|Transitive regain something; common objects include confidence, control, and the lead. Do not add back after regain.|0
school|educational-institution|NOUN|place or institution for education|An institution where children or other learners receive education.|trường học; nhà trường|The village school opened a room for evening literacy classes.|Trường học trong làng mở một phòng dành cho lớp xóa mù chữ buổi tối.|Countable for a particular institution; at school and go to school often describe participation without an article.|0
school|teaching-period|NOUN|time spent in regular classes|The time during which regular classes take place at a school.|giờ học; buổi học ở trường|We met at the gate when school finished for the day.|Chúng tôi gặp nhau ở cổng khi buổi học trong ngày kết thúc.|Uncountable in school starts or finishes and after school; this names scheduled education rather than the building.|1
